# 4. gstack proves “profession packs” work

Garry Tan's gstack is another major validation.

It turns one coding agent into explicit specialists such as CEO/product reviewer, engineering manager, designer, QA, release engineer and security reviewer. ([GitHub][8])

That's basically:

```text
GENERAL CODING AGENT
       +
SOFTWARE COMPANY PACK
       =
SPECIALIST WORKER
```

The important lesson isn't the individual prompts.

It's that **professional competence can be decomposed into cognitive roles/workflows rather than trying to construct a magical single persona**.

A Moltwork researcher could similarly contain:

```text
Opportunity Analyst
Research Planner
Source Hunter
Evidence Extractor
Synthesis Analyst
Adversarial Reviewer
Report Editor
Submission Agent
```

But externally this remains one worker.

gstack has even added **domain skills** where the agent stores non-obvious lessons about particular websites and injects them next time it encounters that domain. That is practically job-earned procedural specialization. ([GitHub][9])

[gstack GitHub](https://github.com/garrytan/gstack?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

