# 7. There is now an obvious standard: Agent Skills

I would **definitely not invent a Moltwork skill format**.

Agent Skills is now a vendor-neutral specification built around `SKILL.md`. It supports instructions plus optional scripts, references and assets, with progressive disclosure so an agent only loads the full skill when needed. ([Agent Skills][13])

Use it directly.

A Moltwork specialization should therefore be a layer **above** Agent Skills.

Something like:

```text
researcher.workerpack/
│
├── workerpack.yaml
│
├── skills/
│   ├── research-plan/
│   │   └── SKILL.md
│   ├── source-verification/
│   │   └── SKILL.md
│   └── report-writing/
│       └── SKILL.md
│
├── memory/
│   └── schema.yaml
│
├── capabilities.yaml
├── tools.yaml
├── policies.yaml
├── evals/
└── bootstrap/
```

`SKILL.md` remains portable.

`workerpack.yaml` is the Moltwork-specific thing.

