# WorkRun should be the fundamental learning unit

This is where AWM is especially useful.

Agent Workflow Memory showed that agents can extract reusable task workflows from previous trajectories and selectively use them on future jobs; it reported substantial gains on WebArena and Mind2Web. ([arXiv][15])

So don't do:

```text
conversation
→ dump into vector DB
```

Do:

```text
WorkRun
│
├── task
├── context
├── plan
├── actions
├── capabilities_used
├── outputs
├── verifier_results
├── submission
├── external_feedback
├── acceptance
├── payment
└── metrics
        ↓
 Experience Distiller
        ↓
┌────────────┬───────────────┬────────────────┐
fact memory  workflow memory specialist skill
```

**Raw history remains immutable.**

Derived memory can change.

That separation will matter enormously later.

