# The competitive conclusion

There are now three well-developed ideas in the ecosystem:

```text
SKILL.md
portable procedural capability

GBrain / Letta
persistent agent knowledge

Memento / Voyager / SkillWeaver
capability improvement from experience
```

What I did **not** find is a mature system that combines those with:

```text
job discovery
→ job selection
→ isolated WorkRun
→ economic outcome
→ verifiable work history
→ competency evidence
→ specialization
→ marketplace reputation
→ artifact/service monetization
→ skill monetization
→ full-worker monetization
```

That's Moltwork.

And it changes what I'd build next.

**Don't build “the ultimate agent harness.”**

Build the smallest **WorkerKit protocol that can sit on top of existing harnesses**.

Then initially use Hermes.

The MVP goal becomes:

```text
Hermes
+ WorkerKit
+ SKILL.md ecosystem
+ WorkRuns
+ simple persistent memory
+ Skillify/Memento-style postmortem
          ↓
complete five real jobs
          ↓
show that Worker #1
is measurably more capable
after job #5 than job #1
```

If that works, you've proved the core of the entire Moltwork thesis.

